"""
patch_L291_9_earth_step3_20260909.py -- the Earth exhibit, step 3 (gallery repo)

Built on gallery 23054535e3bf742e692f2f3b8bfd4e4eb1f85e2d
at https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/tonyquintanilla.github.io (main),
orrery d39cf27c76dc933a3ee3f8d56fd159e877dcd26d (read only, not edited).
Ledger: L-291 (step 3, on the eleven sourced features), L-305 (the
magnetosphere stays a NAMED absence), L-303 (the card model, built in
patch_L303_1). Protocol v3.55. Design: PREDESIGN_earth_exhibit_20260906.md.

WHAT THIS DOES -- seven files edited, three created, one run.

  interactive.html?exhibit=earth exists after this. The Sun room is
  unchanged in what it draws; its chrome now takes its title, arrival
  half-range, Python driver and scene composition from a table
  (EXHIBITS) with two rows. The sun* function names stay.

  gallery/earth_geometry.js (NEW) -- the four things the Earth room
  needs that no served row describes on its own, each from served
  inputs: the rotation axis and equator (served IAU pole), the direction
  to the Sun (Earth's Horizons elements in the cache, propagated to the
  epoch by the assembler), the terminator with a subsolar marker
  (geometry perpendicular to that direction; no lighting model), and the
  Moon's trusted arc (the served trust window, propagated by the same
  solver that places the Moon). It also composes the room: served
  shells, these four, the Moon faint, the arrival policy, and the
  magnetosphere as a named absence for the drawer.

  gallery/feature_renderers.js -- the geostationary ring draws, as the
  shape "equatorial_ring" inside the shell-set renderer, tilted by the
  served pole. Two things found in passing and fixed because Earth
  renders them: belts larger than the arrival frame now go to the drawer
  as shells do (the inner belt at 1.5 R_earth was drawing lit and
  setting the frame), and the belts get their served link and their
  "flux PEAK, not an edge" note in the hover and the i-panel. The served
  source string now rides in every trace's meta so the i-panel can show
  it under the link.

  documentation/smoke_features.js -- one expected warning (the
  magnetosphere), 14 Earth traces, GEO in Earth's equatorial plane at
  the served radius. documentation/smoke_earth_geometry.js (NEW, 26
  checks) and documentation/payload_earth_scene.json (NEW, the driver's
  real output against the served cache of 2026-09-08) -- the Earth room
  composed headless. gallery_maintenance_run.py runs it as a gating
  row, "Earth scene geometry", and serves earth_geometry.js in --live.

  tools/json_converter.py -- Studio's New Interactive Card picker reads
  the rooms from the EXHIBITS table (it read `EXHIBIT === "..."`, which
  this patch removes). data/objects_config.json and
  documentation/payload_earth.json -- the GEO row's note no longer says
  the ring needs a renderer.

THREE THINGS THE HANDOFF HAD WRONG, found by running, not reading:
  - The driver spec "objects Earth and Moon, center Earth" is rejected
    by the resolver: Earth is stored relative to the Sun. The room is
    objects ["moon"], center "earth"; Earth's shells arrive by the
    resolver's centre-features path (L-234).
  - The Moon's served trust window is 3.40 days, not 3.37. The arc
    reads it from the record; no number is typed.
  - The inner radiation belt drew lit on arrival (above).

WHAT THIS DOES NOT DO
  The magnetosphere (L-305, its own build, both repos). Steps 4-8 of
  the build order: this patch's checks run here; Mode 5 is yours.

HOW TO RUN
  Save to the GALLERY repo root. Open in VS Code and press Run. Then run
  gallery_maintenance_run.py (offline; expect 6 of 6), commit, push,
  report the SHA, then run it again with --live.

GUARDS
  Seven files read in binary mode, LF-normalised, md5 checked against
  23054535. Every edit must match exactly once. The three new files must
  not already exist. Nothing is written unless everything passes.
  Inserted text is ASCII-only, LF. Undo is Discard Changes in GitHub
  Desktop.

Written September 2026 with Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.
"""
